<title>NEW ZEALAND: TransAlta posts maiden half-yr profit.</title>
<headline>TransAlta posts maiden half-yr profit.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr result to March 31.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    7.21 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 3.25 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				  nil vs n/a</p>
<p>    Turnover				  125.53 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    13.45 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Tax					   5.68 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Equity earnings		  debit  0.56 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	221.69 vs n/a</p>
<p>Note - TransAlta New Zealand Ltd is an electricity supply company formed from the merger of EnergyDirect Ltd and Wellington's Capital Power in 1996.</p>
<p>Canada's TransAlta Corp owns 62.7 percent of TransAlta New Zealand.</p>
<p>When TransAlta NZ listed on October 1, 1996, the company forecast a NZ$4.2 million profit for the six months to March 31.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
